STABLE
------
=== Require PostgreSQL 12 or newer
extension_drop pulls in cat_tools, and cat_tools 0.3.0 and newer require PostgreSQL 12.

=== Fix bug where extension could not be dropped
The extension now requires extension_drop and trunklet 0.3.3 or later, neither of which 0.2.0 required. Updating from trunklet-format 0.2.0 (PostgreSQL 12 or later) requires trunklet >= 0.3.3:

* If you are on trunklet 0.2.1 or later, run `ALTER EXTENSION trunklet UPDATE;` first, then `CREATE EXTENSION extension_drop CASCADE;` and `ALTER EXTENSION "trunklet-format" UPDATE;`.
* trunklet 0.2.0 has no update path to later versions: drop and recreate it (this also drops trunklet-format and any trunklet data), then install trunklet-format at the stable version.

=== Add optional parameters
A parameter written as `%name%Os` or `%name%OL` may be absent from the parameters, in which case it is treated as NULL. Identifiers (`I`) cannot be optional.

=== Other changes
* `extract_parameters()` returns NULL instead of an error when none of the requested parameters are present.
* Template parse errors report the position in the template.
